## Two gaps this split does not cover

**Corpus authoring has no owner.** Features 4 and 7 are both hard-blocked on it, and it's writing work rather than code — 15–20 ICAR-sourced docs, dated and cited, each carrying structured `distinguishing_cues` with the pest or disease it discriminates from. Nobody in the six is assigned to it. Suggestion: Shruthi and Thaariha split it in the first six hours, since Shruthi's voice work is blocked on the app existing anyway and Thaariha is the one who'll suffer if the corpus is thin.

**The registered-use table has no owner.** Feature 8 is unbuildable without it — active ingredient, crop, registered target, dosage range, PHI, re-entry period, sourced from CIB&RC and state package-of-practices. Even twenty rows covering the common paddy products is enough to demo. Suggestion: Shreekumar authors it alongside the schema, since he owns the lookup anyway. Assign at hour 0 or it will be discovered missing at hour 20.

