## Checkpoints

| Checkpoint | Hour | Check | If it fails |
|---|---|---|---|
| A | 2–6 | Has every name pushed a commit today? | Reassign that block immediately. Do not wait. |
| B | 10 | Does diagnose → gate → advise → follow-up → escalate run end to end on seed data? | All tier 2/3/4 work pauses. Everyone on the core loop. |
| C | 16 | Does the corpus have real content with distinguishing_cues, and does the registered-use table exist? | Hand-write both. Feature 4 and feature 8 both die without them. |
| D | 24 | Is the officials dashboard visibly working, even thin? | Keep the map, drop the analytics. |

Checkpoint A deserves a note. Three of the six names — Shreekumar, Tharun and Thaariha — were at zero or near-zero commits in the last audit, and this split hands them the core backend, the app, and the intelligence layer. That's not a reason to reassign now; people take on more when the work is theirs and the scope is clear. It is a reason to run checkpoint A on time and act on it the same hour, because the three highest-consequence tracks are also the three with the least track record.

## Hard freeze

Hour 29: nothing new merges. 29–32 bug fixes and seed data only. 32–36 two timed rehearsals — if the second doesn't run clean, that's the version you demo.

## Cut order

Farm health (11) → helpline screen (13) → nearby-farm alerts (6) → dashboard analytics, keep the map (15) → voice output, fall back to text with a TTS button (9).

**Never cut:** the confidence gate, the gate object, the Doubt Doctor, "what to avoid" ordering, the IPM ladder with PHI, the label check's veto-not-endorsement rule, mandatory inspection tasks on alerts, and the core diagnose → advise → follow-up → escalate loop.
